#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:18
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:20
msgid ""
"Docusaurus is a project for easily building, deploying, and maintaining "
"open source project websites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:22
msgid ""
"**Simple to Start** Docusaurus is built to be easy to [get up and "
"running](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/installation.html) in as little "
"time possible. We've built Docusaurus to handle the website build process"
" so you can focus on your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:23
msgid ""
"**Localizable** Docusaurus ships with [localization "
"support](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/translation.html) via CrowdIn. "
"Empower and grow your international community by translating your "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:24
msgid ""
"**Customizable** While Docusaurus ships with the key pages and sections "
"you need to get started, including a home page, a docs section, a "
"[blog](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/blog.html), and additional support "
"pages, it is also [customizable](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/custom-"
"pages.html) as well to ensure you have a site that is [uniquely "
"yours](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/api-pages.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:26
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:28
msgid ""
"Docusaurus is available as the [`docusaurus` "
"package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/docusaurus) on "
"[npm](https://www.npmjs.com)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:30
msgid ""
"We have also released the [`docusaurus-init` "
"package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/docusaurus-init) to make [getting "
"started](https://docusaurus.io/docs/en/installation.html) with Docusaurus"
" even easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:32
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:34
msgid ""
"We've released Docusaurus because it helps us better scale and support "
"the many OSS projects at Facebook. We hope that other organizations can "
"benefit from the project. We are thankful for any contributions from the "
"community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:36
msgid "[Code of Conduct](https://code.fb.com/codeofconduct)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:38
msgid ""
"Facebook has adopted a Code of Conduct that we expect project "
"participants to adhere to. Please read [the full "
"text](https://code.fb.com/codeofconduct) so that you can understand what "
"actions will and will not be tolerated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:40
msgid "Contributing Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:42
msgid ""
"Read our [contributing "
"guide](https://github.com/facebook/docusaurus/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md)"
" to learn about our development process, how to propose bugfixes and "
"improvements, and how to build and test your changes to Docusaurus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:44
msgid "Beginner Friendly Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docusaurus_README.md:46
#, python-format
msgid ""
"To help you get your feet wet and get you familiar with our contribution "
"process, we have a list of [beginner friendly "
"bugs](https://github.com/facebook/docusaurus/labels/good%20first%20issue)"
" that might contain smaller issues to tackle first. This is a great place"
" to get started."
msgstr ""

